  <penalty type="severeCollision" name="Severe Collision" code="SC" description="If, in the judgement of the Umpire, there is severe contact between (a) boats, (b) oars and boats or (c) boats/oars and rowers, penalties may be applied. Forcing another boat into a bridge or off the racecourse is also considered a Severe Collision. Incidental or minor contact between boats or oars and boats, is not." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty type="nonYield" name="Non-Yield Interference" code="NY" description="When an overtaking boat closes to within 1 boat length of the stern of the boat ahead (and continues to close) and there is no visible effort on the part of the boat ahead to yield (where yielding can be done safely), a penalty is assessed the overtaken boat." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty type="poorCrossing" name="Poor Crossing Violation" code="PC" description="Any action by a crossing crew that causes a racing crew to slow down to avoid a collision or to alter course is considered Poor Crossing, for which they may be assessed a penalty." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty type="travelLane" name="Travel Lane Violation" code="TL" description="Non-racing boats entering the race course may be penalized for each course buoy cut. Non-racing boats interfering with a racing boat will be severely penalized." assessment="10"/>
  <penalty type="disregardForSafety" name="Disregard for Safety Violation" code="SV" description="A crew that acts in a way that demonstrates a blatant and severe disregard for their safety or the safety of others will receive a 60 second penalty or face disqualification (imposed by the jury). Traffic violations such as entering the race course from the travel lane may fall into this category." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty type="unsportsmanlikeConduct" name="Unsportsmanlike Conduct" code="UC" description="Gross, directed profanity, abusive language, or other actions that violate the bounds of civil conduct will be reported to the Jury and may result in either a reprimand or penalty." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty type="startOrder" name="Start Order Violation" code="SO" description="Entering the starting chute in the wrong order is grounds for a penalty. This includes boats that are late to the starting line and therefore asked to start at the end of their event. A boat that is so late to the start that it cannot row in its event may be excluded." assessment="30"/>
  <penalty type="bridgeArch" name="Arch Violation" code="AR" description="Rowing through an out-of-bounds arch." assessment="60"/>
  <penalty name="Buoy Violation" code="BV" description="Passing on the wrong side of buoys (e.g., green, orange, white), often with increased penalties for repeat offenses." assessment="10"/>
</tdi:TimingRegatta>
